                        "glosses": [
                            "To express as an analogy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0d5852a-411a-4d28-9e7d-f880d08d914d",
                                "sense_id": "e469c471-6f12-3a46-83c0-bbb8e8337b1a",
                                "text": "The teacher analogised swotting for an exam in terms of marathon training."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "632d7df1-21b3-3b90-b6ce-cbcedb2a6ba5",
                        "entry_id": "30d02129-ff1b-3617-a4e3-35f370e196a4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To treat one thing as analogous to another."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b12507c-af2c-4413-a286-dfc669c94c1d",
                                "sense_id": "632d7df1-21b3-3b90-b6ce-cbcedb2a6ba5",
                                "text": "Repulsion over polygamy is so ingrained in the American consciousness — analogizing it to slavery, the Republican platform of 1856 called it one of the country’s “twin relics of barbarism” — that judgmentally reveling in the exotic perversions of “Big Love” feels like something on the order of a national right."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb6cfb49-e1d9-4890-9602-223e179cac54",
                                "sense_id": "632d7df1-21b3-3b90-b6ce-cbcedb2a6ba5",
                                "text": "Cruz was obviously analogizing Bernie Sanders to the Bolsheviks and Hillary Clinton to the Mensheviks. The oleaginous Texan is an erudite slyboots, but his history is off-kilter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6614a027-6118-4127-9a88-ee74276e02df",
                                "sense_id": "632d7df1-21b3-3b90-b6ce-cbcedb2a6ba5",
                                "text": "Writing objective history or raising a teenager may be like trying to nail Jell-O to a wall, as those and other challenging tasks have been popularly analogized."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83e429e6-09a6-499f-a9e3-aa3849006a9c",
                                "sense_id": "632d7df1-21b3-3b90-b6ce-cbcedb2a6ba5",
                                "text": "Nance and the United States analogize any responsive authorization that follows a successful lethal injection challenge to responsive appropriations that would follow a successful Section 1983 claim for improved health care."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
